# Speed first

Treat speed as the highest priority: site performance, agent turn time, and getting to a working result.

- Do the smallest change that solves the request. No extra files, refactors, or docs unless asked.
- Batch reads and edits. Skip recaps, preambles, and optional questions when the next step is clear.
- Prefer the existing stack and patterns. Do not add libraries or abstraction for cleanliness.
- For the public site, keep pages fast: no extra client JS, no heavy images without compression, no blocking work on the critical path.
- Verify only what changed. Stop when it works.
